From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-lenovo-q706f: bring back the AS33970 capture link

Needs 0011 (driver registers its DAI without firmware and never downloads on
its own). Re-enables the DSP node and the "SENARY Capture" DAI link that 0002
removed. Without a firmware download the link exists but cannot be opened;
the regular microphones (WCD938x, "WCD Capture") do not depend on it.

Apply only together with the owner's decision to load the DSP firmware.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts	2026-11-13 13:17:15.658998270 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts	2026-11-13 13:18:53.684632282 +0200
@@ -2143,18 +2143,3 @@
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8250/q706f/venus.mbn";
 	status = "okay";
 };
-
-/*
- * Bring-up: the AS33970 microphone DSP does not answer on this unit and its
- * driver would rewrite the DSP flash. Keep it off and drop its capture link so
- * the sound card (speakers) can register.
- */
-&as33970 {
-	status = "disabled";
-};
-
-&sound {
-	pinctrl-0 = <&pri_tdm_active>;
-
-	/delete-node/ senary-capture-dai-link;
-};
